Description: CVE-2026-63382 - Fix HTTP request smuggling in evhttp.
 Two related hardening changes for the evhttp HTTP parser (GHSA-q39v-w2g7-gr8j):
 .
 1. Treat CRLF strictly in HTTP chunk-size lines. Per RFC 9112 a bare LF must
    not be accepted as a chunk terminator, so the chunk-size reader now uses
    EVBUFFER_EOL_CRLF_STRICT instead of EVBUFFER_EOL_CRLF.
 .
 2. Tighten acceptable Transfer-Encoding / Content-Length header combinations.
    Previously evhttp accepted a wide variety of combinations of
    Content-Length and Transfer-Encoding and did not fully parse
    Transfer-Encoding per the RFC. When used as an HTTP proxy this could
    enable request smuggling attacks. The parser now rejects requests that
    carry both Transfer-Encoding and Content-Length, duplicate Content-Length
    headers, and non-terminal or malformed "chunked" transfer-codings.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/libevent/libevent/commit/10abb34b8dc3e1184de315dd261ce4b77563cda6
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/libevent/libevent/commit/ac38703b2d312200c4f967f02936af0118d384a0
Author: Nick Mathewson <nickm@torproject.org>
Bug: https://github.com/libevent/libevent/security/advisories/GHSA-q39v-w2g7-gr8j
Last-Update: 2026-08-23
