Description: CVE-2026-63388 - Fix heap out-of-bounds write in bufferevent via AF_UNIX+http+NDEBUG
 bufferevent stored the saved connection address in a union of
 struct sockaddr_in6 / struct sockaddr_in, which is too small to hold a
 struct sockaddr_un. When an AF_UNIX address was passed (notably through the
 http code path), bufferevent_socket_set_conn_address_() memcpy'd more bytes
 than the destination could hold, causing a heap out-of-bounds write. The
 oversized-addrlen case was only guarded by EVUTIL_ASSERT(), which is compiled
 out under -DNDEBUG, so release builds performed the overflowing copy silently.
 .
 This backports upstream commit 52057cb33d0c20c0a0453fbabe6c0c96854931b9
 (release-2.1.13-stable): the conn_address union is replaced with a
 struct sockaddr_storage large enough for any supported address family, and
 bufferevent_socket_set_conn_address_() now returns an error code instead of
 asserting when addrlen is too large. Both call sites
 (bufferevent_connect_getaddrinfo_cb() in bufferevent_sock.c and
 evhttp_get_request_connection() in http.c) are updated to check the return
 value and fail the connection cleanly.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/libevent/libevent/commit/52057cb33d0c20c0a0453fbabe6c0c96854931b9
Author: Azat Khuzhin <azat@libevent.org>
Last-Update: 2026-08-24
