Description: CVE-2026-63384 - Fix integer overflow in evtag_unmarshal_header
 evrpc: Fix integer overflow in evtag_unmarshal_header (CWE-190).
 On platforms where int is 32-bit, decoding a tag header whose payload
 length exceeds INT_MAX could cause evtag_unmarshal_header() to return a
 negative value (the ev_uint32_t length is returned via an int result),
 leading to bad/oversized allocations or denial of service in code that
 consumes the returned length. The fix rejects payload lengths larger
 than INT_MAX by returning -1 before the length is used.
 Fixes GHSA-45c6-qx49-89m8.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/libevent/libevent/commit/109c16499282959d70f56ec3baf4c8b1e6646bda
Author: libevent maintainers
Last-Update: 2026-08-23
---
--- a/event_tagging.c
+++ b/event_tagging.c
@@ -445,7 +445,7 @@ evtag_unmarshal_header(struct evbuffer *evbuf, ev_uint32_t *ptag)

 	if (decode_tag_internal(ptag, evbuf, 1 /* dodrain */) == -1)
 		return (-1);
-	if (evtag_decode_int(&len, evbuf) == -1)
+	if (evtag_decode_int(&len, evbuf) == -1 || len > INT_MAX)
 		return (-1);

 	if (evbuffer_get_length(evbuf) < len)
--- a/include/event2/tag.h
+++ b/include/event2/tag.h
@@ -64,6 +64,8 @@ void evtag_init(void);
 /**
    Unmarshals the header and returns the length of the payload

+   Returns an error if the payload length is above INT_MAX.
+
    @param evbuf the buffer from which to unmarshal data
    @param ptag a pointer in which the tag id is being stored
    @returns -1 on failure or the number of bytes in the remaining payload.
Description: CVE-2026-63385 - http: Reject headers containing CRLF (HTTP header injection)
 evhttp_header_is_valid_value() previously permitted header values that
 contained CR/LF sequences as long as they were followed by a space or tab,
 accepting the obs-fold line-folding construct deprecated in RFC 9112. For
 certain proxy chains this created an HTTP header/response injection
 opportunity (CWE-444, request/response smuggling).
 .
 This backport rejects any header value that contains a CR or LF character
 outright, matching the upstream fix. The accompanying regression test in
 test/regress_http.c is updated so that a folded value is now expected to be
 rejected while an equivalent unfolded value is still accepted.
 .
 Note: this addresses the CRLF/obs-fold header-injection finding of
 GHSA-jcwh-pvf2-73p2. The advisory's separate %00 URI-decoding
 path-truncation finding has no upstream fix available and is not covered here.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/libevent/libevent/commit/758be0c0f69c1934ef9a84ab39e9f9e5fde2e6d0
Bug: https://github.com/libevent/libevent/security/advisories/GHSA-jcwh-pvf2-73p2
Author: Nick Mathewson <nickm@torproject.org>
Last-Update: 2026-08-23
---
--- a/http.c
+++ b/http.c
@@ -1955,13 +1955,11 @@
 {
 	const char *p = value;

-	while ((p = strpbrk(p, "\r\n")) != NULL) {
-		/* we really expect only one new line */
-		p += strspn(p, "\r\n");
-		/* we expect a space or tab for continuation */
-		if (*p != ' ' && *p != '\t')
-			return (0);
+	if (strpbrk(p, "\r\n") != NULL) {
+		/* Reject any header containing CR or LF. */
+		return (0);
 	}
+
 	return (1);
 }

